  "name": "cot",
  "notes": [
    "Socrata dataset 72hh-3qpy (Disaggregated - Futures Only), all provider columns, market codes {'gold': '088691', 'silver': '084691', 'copper': '085692', 'crude': '067651'}, report dates from 2010-01-01.",
    "release_utc = 15:30 US/Eastern on the scheduled release day, converted to UTC. The day comes from the captured CFTC release-schedule pages (release_source = cftc_schedule:...) and otherwise from the rule 'Friday after the Tuesday report date; a federal holiday on Wednesday-Friday of that week moves the release to the following Monday' (release_source = rule:...). The captured schedules are tentative: publication was suspended during the 2013, 2018-19 and 2025 lapses in appropriations and delayed in Feb-Mar 2023 (ION cyber incident); see the captured Historical Special Announcements page.",
    "loaded_utc = Socrata :created_at for rows loaded one report at a time (15:30 ET on the actual publication day, matching the CFTC's 2025 catch-up table); null for rows that came in with a bulk load (days with >= 50 rows for one market: ['2022-08-01']). Where loaded_utc exists it is the better clock.",
    "available_utc is the best availability evidence per row: loaded_utc where the row was loaded one report at a time, else release_utc. release_caveat marks report weeks whose scheduled day is known to be wrong or uncertain (2013 and 2018-19 lapses, 2023 ION incident, 2025-01-09 day of mourning, 2025 lapse); for 2018-19 release_utc follows the Tuesday/Friday catch-up rule stated in CFTC press release 7864-19 (captured).",
    "TFF (gpe5-46if) skipped: zero rows for all four market codes (captures in parts/cot/tff_evidence.json).",
    "Numbers are float64 as Socrata serves them as strings; provider field names are kept verbatim."
  ],
